        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\section{Introduction}\\label{sec:intro}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "Large language models (LLMs) are used for tasks that range from knowledge-intensive"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "question answering and document summarization to explanation, brainstorming, and"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "creative writing. Across these uses, fluency is not enough: a response must make"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "commitments"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "Hallucination evaluation"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "is therefore a reliability"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "problem, but also a question of what should count as an error in context"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "AA-Omniscience"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "open-weight models"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "That conclusion matters because LLM deployments do not all ask for the same kind"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "of response."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "In factual question answering or source-grounded summarization,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "unsupported content is normally an error. In an explanation, however, an"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "analogy may be useful without being literally true; brainstorming and fiction"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "may invite invention; and hypothesis generation may ask for possibilities that"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "the available evidence leaves unsettled"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\citep{franceschelli_creativity_2024,jiang_survey_2024,rick_supermind_2023}."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "Creativity research commonly distinguishes novelty from usefulness or quality"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\citep{runco_standard_2012,diedrich_are_2015}, while style-transfer research"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "treats the form of a response as a separate, controllable property"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\citep{kang_style_2021}. A metaphor may therefore be valuable precisely because"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "therefore"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "it is not a literal restatement of the source, while a factually correct answer"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "may still fail a requested style. Factuality, source faithfulness, creativity,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "actuality, source faithfulness, creativity,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "and response style consequently answer different evaluation questions."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "and response style consequently answer different evaluation questions"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "The crucial"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "distinction is between introducing a possibility within the task's scope and"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "asserting it as a fact."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "These settings require two judgments"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "settle"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "judgments"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "operationalize"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "contrast"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "label"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "task"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "The museum example does not make factuality or source-faithfulness evaluation"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "unnecessary; it clarifies their scope. Some tasks ask a model to reproduce facts"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "from external knowledge, whereas others ask it to stay faithful to a supplied"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "document. Still others ask it to solve a problem, explain an idea with an"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "analogy, or write in a particular style. A statement that is not literally"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "supported by the source may be useful in the latter tasks but erroneous in the"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "former. We therefore treat factuality, source faithfulness, creativity, and"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "response style as related but distinct requirements."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "Factuality evaluation compares generated claims with external knowledge"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "sources, whereas source-faithfulness evaluation compares them with a provided"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "source document"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\citep{maynez_faithfulness_2020,kryscinski_evaluating_2020,min_factscore_2023}."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "In the framework developed below, these resources instantiate the task oracle."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\citep{runco_standard_2012,diedrich_are_2015};"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "CreativityPrism, for example, evaluates quality, novelty, and diversity"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\citep{hou_creativityprism_2025}, and recent surveys and task-specific novelty"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "metrics continue to refine these criteria"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\citep{ismayilzada_progress_2024,zhao_assessing_2025,namuduri_genie_2026}."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "These dimensions do not by themselves determine whether a novel factual claim"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "violates a task constraint."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "Two protocols can therefore assign different labels to identical wording when"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "their prompts establish different task conditions."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "\\paragraph{Our position}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "the task's truth contract"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "The signal may be a local hedge, a hypothesis label, a section heading, or a"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ol-cm-change ol-cm-change-c",
          "text": "task-level fictional frame."
        }
      ]
    }
